From: Jesse Casco <jesse.casco@gmail.com>
Subject: [RFC PATCH] clk: qcom: gdsc: unwind domains when registration fails

gdsc_register() leaves previously initialized power domains registered if
a later gdsc_init(), subdomain registration, or provider registration
fails. The caller installs its managed gdsc_unregister() action only
after gdsc_register() succeeds, so that action cannot clean up a failed
registration.

Remove the subdomains already added, then remove all initialized domains.
When initialization itself fails, remove only the earlier domains. Leave
the successful unregister path unchanged; it already removes the domains.

Link: https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260602140934.796697-4-github.com@herrie.org
Signed-off-by: Jesse Casco <jesse.casco@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/clk/qcom/gdsc.c | 15 +++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/gdsc.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/gdsc.c
index b99d70149af34e75a822e3c2d9e1afb2ad921f03..989e3d76012e005c3b4a5bc47d1777370d7bb42b 100644
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gdsc.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gdsc.c
@@ -648,7 +648,7 @@ int gdsc_register(struct gdsc_desc *desc,
 		scs[i]->rcdev = rcdev;
 		ret = gdsc_init(scs[i]);
 		if (ret)
-			return ret;
+			goto err_pm_domain_remove;
 		data->domains[i] = &scs[i]->pd;
 	}
 
@@ -667,10 +667,21 @@ int gdsc_register(struct gdsc_desc *desc,
 			goto err_pm_subdomain_remove;
 	}
 
-	return of_genpd_add_provider_onecell(dev->of_node, data);
+	ret = of_genpd_add_provider_onecell(dev->of_node, data);
+	if (ret)
+		goto err_pm_subdomain_remove;
+
+	return 0;
 
 err_pm_subdomain_remove:
 	gdsc_pm_subdomain_remove(desc, i);
+	i = num;
+
+err_pm_domain_remove:
+	while (i--) {
+		if (scs[i])
+			pm_genpd_remove(&scs[i]->pd);
+	}
 
 	return ret;
 }
